## DESIGN LANGUAGE

Visual hierarchy (apply to every slide):
  Title: fontSize 32-40, bold, color="$textMain"
  Labels: fontSize 12-14, color="$textMuted"
  Body: fontSize 14-16, color="$textMain"
  KPI values: fontSize 32-46, bold, with unit in <Span fontSize="18-22">
  Deltas: color="$positive" for up, color="$negative" for down

Slide structure:
  Root: <VStack w="1280" h="720" padding="48-64" gap="24-36" backgroundColor="$surface">
  Place an accent bar below the title: <Shape shapeType="rect" w="120" h="6" backgroundColor="$accent" />
  Charts: always set explicit w and h that fit within the parent container.
  Account for axis labels — leave 40-60px margin so labels don't overflow.
{% if density_tier in ('standard', 'dense') %}

Card recipe (for KPI tiles, info boxes, feature callouts):
  <VStack grow="1" padding="20-28" gap="8-12" backgroundColor="$surfaceAlt"
    borderRadius="12" border.width="1" border.color="$border"
    borderTop.width="4" borderTop.color="$accent">
  IMPORTANT: border.color="$border" is a SUBTLE hairline (gray/light).
  Only borderTop.color uses "$accent" (the bold colored stripe at top).
  NEVER set border.color="$accent" — that makes the whole card outlined in blue.
  Use grow="1" in HStack rows for even card distribution.

Color tokens:
  $surface=background  $surfaceAlt=cards  $accent=anchors  $textMain=headings
  $textMuted=labels  $positive=good  $negative=bad  $border=outlines (subtle gray)
